  "reconstruction": {
    "text": "For every real inner-product space E and every real kappa,define an extended-nonnegative cost on pairs of phase states by\n  C_kappa(z,zprime)=ENNReal.ofReal(Q_kappa(z-zprime)),\nwhere Q_kappa(x,p)=(1/(2kappa)+1/2)||x||^2+<x,p>+||p||^2 and subtraction is coordinatewise. For z=(x,p),zprime=(xprime,pprime),this is the ENNReal embedding of the nonnegative part of Q_kappa(x-xprime,p-pprime). The definition takes no square root and assumes no lower bound on kappa. It asserts no metric property,integrability or coupling existence.",
